("Retirement and account types","Advanced","🏦","Use workplace and IRA rules that fit your eligibility, tax situation and horizon.",[("Workplace plan","Employer plan may offer matching contribution","401(k) match"),("Traditional/Roth","Tax timing and eligibility differ","Compare treatment"),("Limits","Annual thresholds and catch-ups may change","Check tax-year IRS page")],"A matching contribution can matter, but vesting, fees and plan options also matter.","Is a retirement account the same as an investment?","No. The account wrapper and the investments inside it are different choices.","Check employer plan details and current IRS limits.",["IRS retirement limits","IRS IRA limits","SEC allocation"],["Check match","Check limits","Choose holdings","Review"]),
("Taxes, withholding and records","Advanced","🧮","Tax rules change by year; keep records and use current official tools.",[("Withholding","Tax prepaid from pay","W-4 adjustment"),("Gain and basis","Sale proceeds minus adjusted basis, subject to rules","Stock tax lot"),("Documentation","Forms and transactions support filing","W-2, 1099, receipts")],"A capital gain is not the full sale proceeds; basis and other rules matter.","Does a tax refund mean you made an investment profit?","No. A refund generally reflects payments versus tax liability.","Use the IRS estimator and organize tax documents by year.",["IRS withholding","IRS investments tax","IRS tax help"],["Collect forms","Check basis","Estimate","File"]),
("Insurance and risk protection","Advanced","🛡️","Protect against losses that would be difficult to absorb.",[("Coverage","Policy specifies protected events","Health or liability coverage"),("Deductible","Out-of-pocket before some benefits","Compare policy terms"),("Beneficiary","Named recipient on relevant accounts or policies","Review after life changes")],"A cheaper premium may come with a larger deductible or narrower coverage.","Does every policy with the same name offer the same protection?","No. Terms, exclusions and limits matter.","List key policies, renewal dates, deductibles and beneficiaries.",["NAIC insurance","IRS beneficiary"],["Identify risk","Compare terms","Check beneficiary","Review"]),
